Have you ever wondered what happens to your transaction once it leaves the blockchain?
In most cases, when we talk about privacy, the focus is only on what is visible on the blockchain. But in reality, it's much more complicated. A transaction can leak through multiple stages, mempools, execution, interaction with bots and oracles. Even if the final transaction looks clean, information may be revealed before it is completed

@RialoHQ  has its own approach to transaction privacy. Instead of simply hiding data on the blockchain, the system implements asynchronous transactions that can be paused and resumed, while maintaining full privacy at each stage. This solution makes working with the blockchain familiar and convenient for web2 developers, without unnecessary complexities.

