Rialo’s Stake-for-Service (SfS) offers a structural solution to the economic tension between staked capital and operational costs.

Rather than the manual friction of managing gas balances, SfS programmatically routes staking yield directly to cover service fees based on a user-defined 'Ratio'.

This architecture enables 100% capital efficiency—users no longer need to hold idle liquid cash, as the asset effectively funds its own operation.

Crucially, the resulting credits are non-transferable. This design aligns tokenomics purely with utility, ensuring rewards are consumed for productive work rather than speculative dumping.

