Check this out from Rialo they're fixing a big headache in onchain stuff with Stake-for-Service (SfS). Basically, you got your staking money earning yield on one side, but your apps need constant cash for gas, storage, and all that jazz, right? Without it, wallets go empty, bots crash, and everything stops. Super annoying to keep topping up manually.

But SfS changes the game: It takes that staking yield and turns it straight into an auto payment flow. No more babysitting  yield just pays for your app's costs on the spot, like gas or recurring tasks, without needing offchain bots or anything. Boom, your dApps run forever, costs stay predictable, and the whole onchain world feels self sustaining, like yield actually works for you instead of just sitting there.

This is huge for building real stuff in Web3, no drama. Rialo's onto something fire here. Get in early before it blows up.

